From 8d55282f584b59d96ae20ab66a9176bdb6936666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brendan Lynskey <brendanlynskey@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] target/riscv: add the BRV32P custom extensions

The BRV32P core has a DSP extension, Xbrvdsp, on the custom-0 and custom-1
opcodes: a multiply-accumulate unit with a 40-bit accumulator, saturating
and packed-half arithmetic, four address registers with a bit-reversed
mode, a hardware loop, a packed GF(2^8) multiply and packed arithmetic mod
q for NTTs.

Add it as a vendor extension of the brv32p CPU only, in the way QEMU's
other vendor extensions are done: a cfg flag, a decodetree file gated on
it, and translation routines. The state (accumulator, address registers,
loop count and start, GF polynomial, q, q' and zeta) is in CPURISCVState,
reset as the RTL resets it, and migrated in a subsection. The arithmetic is
in helpers and follows the core's Spike model instruction by instruction.

The last instruction of a hardware loop body (mac.lp, dmac.lp, msu.lp,
lp.end) picks its next pc at run time from the loop registers and ends the
translation block. The loads through an address register step it only after
the load has succeeded, so one that traps leaves it unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Brendan Lynskey <brendanlynskey@googlemail.com>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
